The calculation of $v_{2}$ in this study is carried out at various centrality intervals. The charged particle multiplicity distribution is used to determine the centrality of an event. This distribution is obtained within a pseudo-rapidity range of $|\eta|<$ 0.9 and transverse momentum range of 0.2 $< \pt <$ 3.0 GeV/$\it{c}$ similar to that in STAR experiment at RHIC~\cite{exflow17}. Figure~\ref{fig:refmult} represents the multiplicity distribution for d+Au collisions at $\sqn$ from the AMPT-SM model. The events are categorized into three centrality classes: central (0-10\%), mid-central (10-40\%), and peripheral (40-80\%).
