\begin{note*} \normalfont
    Loregian and Bozapalides defines Lax Kan extensions by asking for an $\mathbf{Isomrphism \ of \ categories}$ between $\mathrm{Strict\text{-}Nat}((\mathrm{lLan}_TF,S)$ and $\mathrm{Lax \text{-}Nat}(T,S \circ F)$, however, we think that we should define lax Kan extensions by asking for a  natural equivalence between $\mathrm{Lax \text{-}Nat}(F,S \circ T)$ and $\mathrm{Pseudo \text{-}Nat}(\mathrm{Lan}_T F,S)$, which is similar to our definition of pseudo-Kan extensions.
