\subsection{Forecasting model}
The forecasting model is a U-Net~\citep{Ronneberger2015UNet}, whose architecture is shown in Fig.~\ref{fig:NNfwd}. The network blocks have a similar design as in the AE, but the convolutional layers contain 250 channels. In the innermost layers in the downscaling part of the network, $3\times3$ kernels are used instead of the larger $7\times7$ ones. Additionally, blocks at the same resolution level are linked via skip connections, enabling the preservation and reuse of fine-scale features throughout the network. The NN was trained to produce 12-hour forecasts, while longer lead times were obtained by iteratively applying the model. A 24-hour forecast and its ERA5 reanalysis counterpart are compared in Fig.~\ref{fig:NNfwd quality}.


