 The algorithm given in \autoref{fig:L1p} is enough to produce usable structured text layouts, but it does not elegantly handle whitespace.
Specifically, preceding whitespace on a line \emph{must} be represented by a fragment.
Futhermore, this fragment is not exempt from wrapping.
In practice, this results in unsightly layouts where preceding whitespace draws unneeded visual attention (e.g., see \autoref{fig:L1p-result-no-spacers}).

