\begin{abstract}
  Let $V$ be a vector space over the finite field $\FF_q$
  with $q$ elements and $\Lambda$ be the image of the Segre geometry $\PG(V)\otimes\PG(V^*)$ in $\PG(V\otimes V^*)$.
  Consider the subvariety $\Lambda_{1}$ of $\Lambda$ represented by the pure tensors $x\otimes \xi$ with $x\in V$ and $\xi\in V^*$ such that $\xi(x)=0$.
  Regarding $\Lambda_1$ %and $\Lambda_{\sigma}$
as a projective system of $\PG(V\otimes V^*)$, we study the linear code $\cC(\Lambda_1)$ %and $\cC(\Lambda_{\sigma})$
arising from it.
%After having determined a general condition to establish
%the minimality of codes arising from embeddings of geometries,
We show that
$\cC(\Lambda_1)$ is a minimal code and we determine its basic parameters,
its  full weight list and its linear automorphism group.  We also give a geometrical characterization of its minimum and second lowest weight codewords as well as of some of the words of maximum weight.
\end{abstract}
