\begin{abstract} 
We consider locally compact subgroups $H$ of the full isometry group $\Isom(\E^n)$ of Euclidean $n$-space which respect the splitting into an orthogonal 
and a translation subgroup. We prove that the conjugator length function of such groups grows linearly. Our theorem applies, in particular, to the Lie group $\Isom(\E^n)$ itself but also to affine Coxeter groups and to split crystallographic groups.
\end{abstract}

