\subsection{Macrocirculation Dynamics}
Figure~\ref{fig:macrocircFlowAndPressure} depicts the flow and pressure in our 1D-0D coupled model described in Section~\ref{sec:macrocirculation} at some sample points on the path from the aorta to the vessels that are coupled with the 3D-1D coupled microcirculation model (see Section~\ref{sec:microcirculation}). The average flows $Q_0$ used in the coupling are indicated by dotted lines. For the given setting assuming $\gamma = 3$ we obtain: 
$$
Q_0 \approx 0.46 \;\frac{\unit{cm^3}}{\unit{s}}.
$$
Based on this value we have for $\Lambda_c$ the following inflow rates:
$$
Q_{r_{c,1}} \approx 8.19 \times 10^{-8} \frac{\unit{cm^3}}{\unit{s}} \text{ and } Q_{r_{c,2}} \approx 5.75 \times 10^{-8} \frac{\unit{cm^3}}{\unit{s}} .
$$
