     \[\tau_{conv} = \frac{519c^2\left(25\frac{D^{10}}{\eta}\right)^t}{\log(1+\frac{\eta}{2D(D+1)})},\]
    % In this case, $\alpha_1^f>0$ and we will find a value of $\tau$ such that we are guaranteed $f^{(t+\tau)} \ge 1$. To find the largest such $\tau$, the worst case to consider is when $\alpha_2^f$ is positive and as large as possible and when $\alpha_1^f$ is positive and as small as possible.
