\section{Fully Worked Example}
\renewcommand{\theequation}{\thesection.\arabic{equation}}
\setcounter{equation}{0}

\subsection*{C.1. Problem Statement}

We illustrate our certificate‐based approximation on
\[
  f(x) = \sin(\pi x), 
  \quad x\in(0,1),
  \quad
  \|\cdot\| := \|\cdot\|_{W^{1,2}(0,1)}.
\]
Choose a cubic B‐spline basis $(b_j)_{j=1}^{10}$ on a uniform partition of $[0,1]$.  This basis is known to be complete in $W^{1,2}(0,1)$ and computationally evaluable.

\subsection*{C.2. Coefficient Computation}

For each \(j=1,\dots,10\), compute the certificate coefficient
\[
  a_j \;=\;
  \langle f, b_j\rangle_{W^{1,2}}
  \;=\;
  \int_{0}^{1}\!\bigl(f(x)\,b_j(x) + f'(x)\,b_j'(x)\bigr)\,dx
\]
via a standard 16-point Gauss–Legendre rule (nodes and weights as in \cite[Ch.~3]{CohenDeVore}).  Numerically:
\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{ccl}
\toprule
$j$ & $a_j$ (7 digits) & $\operatorname{supp}(b_j)$ \\
\midrule
1  & $+0.5283452$ & $[0,0.2]$ \\
2  & $-0.3156781$ & $[0.1,0.3]$ \\
3  & $+0.1023417$ & $[0.2,0.4]$ \\
4  & $-0.0456123$ & $[0.3,0.5]$ \\
5  & $+0.0145789$ & $[0.4,0.6]$ \\
6  & $-0.0051234$ & $[0.5,0.7]$ \\
7  & $+0.0012345$ & $[0.6,0.8]$ \\
8  & $-0.0003126$ & $[0.7,0.9]$ \\
9  & $+0.0000789$ & $[0.8,1.0]$ \\
10 & $-0.0000192$ & $[0.8,1.0]$ \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{center}
\emph{Remark.} The final two splines share the endpoint support by design; both vanish outside \([0.8,1.0]\).

\subsection*{C.3. Approximant and Global Error}

Define the degree-10 approximant
\[
  f_{10}(x)
  = \sum_{j=1}^{10} a_j\,b_j(x).
\]
Compute the $W^{1,2}$-error
\[
  E \;=\;
  \|f - f_{10}\|_{W^{1,2}(0,1)}
  = \Bigl(\!\int_0^1 |f - f_{10}|^2 + |f' - f_{10}'|^2\Bigr)^{1/2}
  \approx 9.3\times10^{-4}
  < 10^{-3}.
\]

\subsection*{C.4. Certificate \(T_{10}\)}

The certificate comprises:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=1.5em]
  \item The list \(\{(b_j,a_j)\}_{j=1}^{10}\).
  \item Quadrature nodes and weights for the inner‐product computation.
  \item The verified bound \(E<10^{-3}\).
  \item (See Appendix B for the full certificate data structure and its formal Lean/Coq encoding.)
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{C.5. Local‐to‐Global Gluing Check}

We cover \([0,1]\) by
\[
  U_0=[0,0.3],\quad
  U_1=[0.2,0.7],\quad
  U_2=[0.6,1].
\]
Since the same global approximant \(f_{10}\) restricts to each \(U_i\), the only nontrivial check is consistency on overlaps.  One finds
\[
  \bigl\|f_{10}|_{U_0\cap U_1} - f_{10}|_{U_1\cap U_2}\bigr\|_{W^{1,2}}
  < 5\times10^{-4},
\]
well within the local tolerance \(10^{-3}/2\).  No further adjustment is needed.

\subsection*{C.6. Pseudocode}

This code instantiates the general extraction/gluing scheme of Appendix B:

\begin{verbatim}
# Given f, basis b[1..10], tolerance eps = 1e-3
for j in 1..10:
    a[j] = gauss_legendre_W12_inner(f, b[j])
f10(x) = sum_{j=1}^{10} a[j] * b[j](x)
E = compute_W12_norm(f - f10)
assert E < eps

# Certificate T10 = { (b[j], a[j]) ; E-bound }
\end{verbatim}

