\abstract{In this paper we provide a mathematical framework based on asymptotic analysis of layer potential operators for determining the existence of subwavelength resonance in elastic metascreen and resonance frequency calculation. We consider the case of high shear modulus contrast between metascreen inclusions and background medium. When the shear modulus of inclusions tends to infinity, we prove the occurrence of subwavelength resonance and demonstrate the dramatic change of scattered field due to subwavelength resonance by calculating approximated field inside inclusions and far-away from metascreen. When the shear modulus of background goes to infinity, we prove the absence of subwavelength resonance.}
